1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,647
Question seven. Highlight: each sold ticket gets a “venue-unique” number used to “identify” that ticket and link showtime and seat.

2
00:00:09,647 --> 00:00:13,476
Useful: uniquely identifying a record = primary key.

3
00:00:13,476 --> 00:00:17,379
Useless: cinema theme — does not change the key role.

4
00:00:17,379 --> 00:00:21,577
Option A. Remark-field text: not guaranteed unique — cut.

5
00:00:21,577 --> 00:00:26,069
Option B. Parity bit: error check, not ticket identity — cut.

6
00:00:26,069 --> 00:00:28,205
Option C. Primary key — keep.

7
00:00:28,205 --> 00:00:33,065
Option D. File-compression parameter: unrelated to identity — cut.

8
00:00:33,065 --> 00:00:37,336
Venue-unique and used to identify — best as a primary key.

9
00:00:37,336 --> 00:00:39,840
Therefore the correct answer is C.

